# scripts/screen_shard.sh keeps the previous report before measure_pi.py
# rewrites it from scratch. Churn, not an artifact - consolidate_screens.py's
# glob ignores it too.
*.json.bak

# Partial Test/ archives for a cloud run - built by hand, tens of GB.
/test_*.zip

# Shard program lists, rewritten from data/tasks.json on every run and carrying
# the corpus digest that produced them. Regenerated, not authored.
data/shards/
data/eval_shards/*.txt
data/**/shards/
data/**/eval_shards/*.txt

# The universe lists. eval_shard.sh rewrites all four from tasks.json on every
# run and stamps each with the corpus digest that produced it, so a tracked copy
# is a stale copy waiting to disagree with the corpus beside it. demo_programs
# is NOT here: eval_shard.sh's help says that one is a draw you write by hand.
data/eval_order.txt
data/sweep_programs.txt
data/trial_programs.txt
data/live_programs.txt
data/**/eval_order.txt
data/**/sweep_programs.txt
data/**/trial_programs.txt
data/**/live_programs.txt

# RUN_DIR: a named run writes to data/<slug>/ and logs/<slug>/ (src/paths.py).
# logs/ is already ignored wholesale by `logs/*` at the top, so only the data
# side needs saying - and it is deliberately NOT ignored. This repo tracks its
# artifacts (133 files under data/), so a run's output should show up in
# `git status` and be committed or discarded on purpose, exactly like the
# default run's. The churn rules above are mirrored one level down so a named
# run ignores the same junk the default run does.
